Description: GPU module set {{ SET }} profile (kernel modules, loader policy)
 GPU FINAL (owner 2026-11-03): the four GPU module sets rebuild the profile
 build of the vendor drivers as modules-only entries on top of the standard
 kernel (daemoncores-kernel). The set the machine runs is chosen AT INSTALL
 (bootc-installer GPU profile selector, P-513a pattern) — the image carries
 no set; the bootc-installer pulls this deb from the APT repo and the loader
 policy lands in /etc/modprobe.d/dc-gpu-{{ SET }}.conf. The in-tree sets
 (gpu-ia, gpu-gaming) conflict with each other: exactly one can be
 installed. The -nvidia variants carry only the loader policy: their in-tree
 modules come from the sibling open set and the NVIDIA open kernel modules
 from the linux-modules-nvidia base deb — one modules-only build per
 profile, one NVIDIA base, four sets.